        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nGeneral structure of highlighter is [already fixed](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/335fdd637e905c5cdb8d7e7a9602e38cea9193af/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L250-L303) and it can define word to be highlighted only via a single Lua pattern. This design choice is both for speed (Lua patterns are *very* fast) and implementation simplicity.\r\n\r\nThe closest to a solution of this task is creating a callable highlighter that constructs a pattern based on its comment structure. A general function might utilize 'commentstring' option.\r\n\r\nA more targeted examples for filetypes are possible inside 'after/ftplugin/lua.lua' with the code similar to [this example in help](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/335fdd637e905c5cdb8d7e7a9602e38cea9193af/doc/mini-hipatterns.txt#L178-L208):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.b.minihipatterns_config = {\r\n  highlighters = {\r\n    todo_in_comment = { pattern = '^%s*%-%-.-()TODO()', group = 'MiniHipatternsTodo' },\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlthough use case seems interesting, I don't think complicating highlighter definition is worth it. Closing as not planned.",
